 Compose complete scenes with setting, action, dialogue, and interiority working together. Develop paragraphs when a thought or encounter needs room. Let exchanges move at their natural pace. Select, compress, and dramatize without flattening the recognizable interaction into a dry synopsis. There is no dialogue quota, paragraph quota, word target, or requirement to expand every source beat. Preserve the consequential story and the character-defining pleasures of the session. End each scene at its real boundary and the chapter where the recorded session ends.
 
